    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Seiya Suzuki**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 75.03. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, with his value bolstered by a rare combination of strong SP skill metrics and a delivery profile that invites high-probability stolen base opportunities. **Brice Turang** (71.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.87) follow closely behind; while **Corbin Carroll** faces a slight platoon headwind against Matthew Boyd, his elite speed remains the catalyst of our roster construction. **Mickey Moniak** (67.05) is our most significant beneficiary of platoon dynamics, as his favorable split against Matt Waldron pushes him into \"Strong\" start territory, helping us hunt for counting stats in a high-leverage spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Griffin Conine** (43.48), who hovered just below our 40-point threshold for active play. While **Griffin Conine** brings decent xwOBA metrics, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a restrictive matchup against Sonny Gray, whose SP skill profile creates too much volatility for our current Roto needs. We are also keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley** (54.66) and **Jose Caballero** (51.19); both are currently in \"Marginal\" territory, and should their confirmed batting orders drift lower than our projections, they are the primary candidates for a mid-day swap to preserve game caps. \n\nManagers should note that today\u2019s entire slate carries elevated variance as we await finalized lineups. We are particularly monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** for potential order movement; any decline in their projected slotting could shift our daily outlook significantly. Furthermore, while **James Wood** remains on the IL, our depth\u2014including prospects like **Edwin Arroyo**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014is prepared to soak up volume if the starters falter. We remain in a holding pattern on **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Cole Young**, keeping them available should an emergency substitution become necessary before first pitch.",
